WEBVTT

00:00:00.585 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.632 --> 00:00:03.470
Today we talk about builder gel.

00:00:03.655 --> 00:00:07.390
Many places call it BIAB, which means builder gel in a bottle.

00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:09.814
It is a service clients ask for a lot,

00:00:09.764 --> 00:00:13.710
because it makes the natural nail both strong and naturally beautiful.

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:18.497
But that same service, done without understanding, lifts, breaks,

00:00:18.447 --> 00:00:20.750
and the client does not come back.

00:00:21.339 --> 00:00:24.749
First, how is builder gel different from gel polish?

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.909
Gel polish is runny and thin, mostly there for color.

00:00:29.256 --> 00:00:33.789
It is flexible and bends with the nail, but it does not make the nail any stiffer.

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:36.829
Builder gel is much thicker, like honey.

00:00:37.338 --> 00:00:40.509
Placed on the nail, it flows out flat by itself;

00:00:40.618 --> 00:00:41.789
it is self leveling.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.109
And when it is cured, it becomes a frame that supports the natural nail.

00:00:46.354 --> 00:00:46.989
In short:

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:50.269
gel polish is the coat, and builder gel is the frame.

00:00:50.944 --> 00:00:52.994
You need to tell two families apart.

00:00:53.238 --> 00:00:55.714
The first family can be removed with acetone:

00:00:56.061 --> 00:01:00.425
most of the gels in a bottle that people call BIAB, and thick bases,

00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:03.154
or rubber bases, belong to this family too.

00:01:03.743 --> 00:01:05.554
The second family is hard gel.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.634
Acetone cannot dissolve it;

00:01:07.887 --> 00:01:09.794
to remove it, you have to file.

00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:13.714
So before you start, read the instructions of the brand carefully:

00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:18.114
how this product is removed, how long it is cured, and under which lamp.

00:01:18.537 --> 00:01:21.794
And for removing it correctly, review the gel removal lesson.

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:24.209
Who is builder gel right for?

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.673
Clients with thin, soft nails that bend easily,

00:01:27.623 --> 00:01:30.236
nails that split into layers at the tip,

00:01:30.186 --> 00:01:33.569
nails that break as soon as they grow a little long.

00:01:34.074 --> 00:01:36.727
The frame keeps the nail from being bent every day,

00:01:36.677 --> 00:01:39.329
so the client can keep the length of her own nails.

00:01:39.755 --> 00:01:41.089
But let me be honest with you:

00:01:41.357 --> 00:01:45.809
builder gel does not make nails grow faster, and it does not cure nails.

00:01:45.974 --> 00:01:49.169
It only protects them, so they do not break while they grow.

00:01:49.832 --> 00:01:51.165
And when should you not do it?

00:01:51.727 --> 00:01:54.205
When the nail has a problem a doctor should look at:

00:01:54.378 --> 00:01:57.967
a nail separating from the nail bed, discolored, thickened,

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.365
or skin around the nail that is swollen,

00:02:00.462 --> 00:02:01.965
red, or has pus.

00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:04.685
When the client has had a gel allergy before:

00:02:04.944 --> 00:02:07.965
itching, redness, blistering around the nails.

00:02:08.314 --> 00:02:10.845
And also nails bitten right down, too short.

00:02:11.121 --> 00:02:13.405
Gel has to bond to the natural nail.

00:02:13.585 --> 00:02:16.842
With too little nail, the gel has little to hold on to,

00:02:16.792 --> 00:02:18.765
and touches the skin more easily.

00:02:19.188 --> 00:02:23.126
For these clients, it is often better to care for the nails for a while,

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.205
so they grow longer,

00:02:24.314 --> 00:02:25.005
and then do it.

00:02:25.544 --> 00:02:27.173
Now the most important part:

00:02:27.494 --> 00:02:28.293
the structure.

00:02:28.952 --> 00:02:32.773
A beautiful builder gel set is not evenly thick, like a plank.

00:02:33.224 --> 00:02:34.213
It has a shape.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:36.373
Thin right at the cuticle.

00:02:36.631 --> 00:02:37.733
Thin at the tip.

00:02:38.143 --> 00:02:40.773
And thickest at one point, called the apex.

00:02:41.374 --> 00:02:42.369
Why thick there?

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:46.849
Every day, the client types, opens lids, does up buttons.

00:02:47.278 --> 00:02:50.849
The nail gets pushed upward, and it tends to break in one place:

00:02:51.094 --> 00:02:54.369
where the nail leaves the skin bed, where the free edge begins.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.969
That is the stress area.

00:02:56.397 --> 00:03:00.049
The apex must sit right over the stress area, just slightly behind it.

00:03:00.558 --> 00:03:04.849
The gel is thickest there, like a supporting beam, so the nail is not bent.

00:03:04.991 --> 00:03:08.594
But if the gel layer is completely flat, with no apex,

00:03:08.544 --> 00:03:11.489
the nail still flexes up and down every day,

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.329
and the gel gradually lifts.

00:03:13.949 --> 00:03:18.070
Looking at the nail from the tip, it has a curve, like the letter C.

00:03:18.544 --> 00:03:22.069
The gel must follow that curve, evenly on both sides.

00:03:22.497 --> 00:03:26.076
Along the side walls of the nail, the gel is thin and neat,

00:03:26.026 --> 00:03:28.230
straight along the edge of the nail,

00:03:28.403 --> 00:03:31.110
not bulging, and not flowing onto the skin.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.870
For every set, practice looking from three directions:

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.910
from above, from the side, and from the tip.

00:03:38.463 --> 00:03:40.232
There is something that happens a lot:

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:44.232
the client comes back after a week, and the gel has lifted at the cuticle.

00:03:44.818 --> 00:03:47.032
Usually it is for one of four reasons.

00:03:47.205 --> 00:03:49.352
One, the prep was not thorough:

00:03:49.546 --> 00:03:52.174
the nail still had oil, moisture or shine,

00:03:52.124 --> 00:03:55.672
or a thin layer of skin was left stuck to the nail plate.

00:03:56.156 --> 00:04:01.192
Two, the gel touched the skin, flowing into the corners or onto the cuticle area.

00:04:01.436 --> 00:04:04.712
The skin grows, pushes the gel up, and it lifts.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.542
Three, the gel was too thick at the edge,

00:04:07.492 --> 00:04:10.712
forming a ridge that pops off at the slightest catch.

00:04:10.977 --> 00:04:13.112
And four, there was no apex:

00:04:13.381 --> 00:04:17.992
the nail flexed up and down every day, until the gel could not take it any more.

00:04:18.607 --> 00:04:19.748
Now about heat.

00:04:20.136 --> 00:04:23.028
When gel cures under the lamp, it gives off heat.

00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:25.348
The thicker the layer, the more heat.

00:04:25.919 --> 00:04:28.168
Builder gel is thicker than gel polish,

00:04:28.118 --> 00:04:31.268
so clients often feel burning in the first few seconds.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.618
Many lamps have a low heat mode,

00:04:33.568 --> 00:04:37.828
or the brand recommends a quick flash cure of a few seconds to set the gel,

00:04:38.012 --> 00:04:39.028
then the full cure.

00:04:39.371 --> 00:04:41.028
Follow the instructions of the brand.

00:04:41.292 --> 00:04:45.267
If the client feels heat, let her take the hand out for a few seconds,

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:46.388
then put it back in,

00:04:46.577 --> 00:04:48.228
and still cure for the full time.

00:04:48.523 --> 00:04:50.388
Do not make the client put up with pain.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.708
Too much heat can damage the nail bed.

00:04:53.099 --> 00:04:55.988
Better to do two moderate layers than one very thick one.

00:04:56.651 --> 00:04:58.802
On allergy, just three reminders.

00:04:59.141 --> 00:05:02.802
Uncured gel must never touch the skin of the client, or your own.

00:05:03.311 --> 00:05:04.962
The gel must be fully cured:

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:08.201
the type of lamp the brand recommends, the full time,

00:05:08.151 --> 00:05:10.082
and no layers that are too thick.

00:05:10.514 --> 00:05:13.296
And filing dust must be extracted, not blown,

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:17.362
because dust from gel that is not fully cured causes allergies too.

00:05:17.604 --> 00:05:22.082
In Europe, nail products containing HEMA must say clearly on the label:

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:26.002
for professional use only, and can cause an allergic reaction.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:31.442
Nail products containing TPO are already banned, so check the stock in your salon.

00:05:31.712 --> 00:05:33.682
Rules differ from country to country.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:38.082
For more detail on allergy, review the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:05:38.608 --> 00:05:39.853
Then there are infills.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:43.539
As the nail grows out, the gel slowly moves towards the tip,

00:05:43.489 --> 00:05:44.893
taking the apex with it.

00:05:45.146 --> 00:05:48.017
The frame shifts forward, the nail becomes top heavy,

00:05:47.967 --> 00:05:49.933
and it breaks and lifts more easily.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:54.093
So usually every three to four weeks, the client should come back for an infill:

00:05:54.252 --> 00:05:57.521
file the old layer thinner, cover the new growth at the cuticle,

00:05:57.471 --> 00:05:59.533
and rebuild the apex in the right place.

00:05:59.697 --> 00:06:01.859
If the old layer is still well bonded,

00:06:01.809 --> 00:06:04.526
you can do many infills without removing it all,

00:06:04.476 --> 00:06:07.693
so the natural nail is spared from removal after removal.

00:06:08.329 --> 00:06:10.494
Finally, be honest with the client.

00:06:10.923 --> 00:06:13.694
Do not promise that gel will make her nails healthier.

00:06:13.874 --> 00:06:14.414
Say:

00:06:14.684 --> 00:06:18.094
this layer keeps your nails from breaking, so they can grow longer.

00:06:18.501 --> 00:06:19.374
Tell the client:

00:06:19.641 --> 00:06:22.894
if it lifts, do not peel it or pry it off yourself;

00:06:23.174 --> 00:06:24.254
come back to the salon.

00:06:24.799 --> 00:06:26.974
Wear gloves when washing up or cleaning.

00:06:27.402 --> 00:06:29.934
And apply cuticle oil around the nails every day.

00:06:30.181 --> 00:06:33.614
When clients understand, they help you look after their nails.

00:06:34.243 --> 00:06:34.815
You see.

00:06:35.064 --> 00:06:37.215
Builder gel is not hard for the hands.

00:06:37.386 --> 00:06:38.655
It is hard for the head:

00:06:39.058 --> 00:06:42.786
understanding where the nail takes the stress, where to put the high point,

00:06:42.736 --> 00:06:44.895
and how to keep the gel away from the skin.

00:06:45.396 --> 00:06:47.855
Once you understand it, your hands will follow.

00:06:48.269 --> 00:06:51.375
In the practice lesson, we will go step by step together.

00:06:51.638 --> 00:06:54.175
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:54.352 --> 00:06:55.135
See you next time.
